(:include "tiers/melee.domain")
(:include "tiers/follow.domain")
(:include "tiers/idle.domain")

// Pet follower: fight what threatens it, else follow its leader, else idle.
//
// Teaches: the follow tier as a middle priority, re-entrant across replans (catch up / keep waiting / loiter near
// the leader), the leader given as a fact by the host (who tamed or summoned the pet), guards on every root branch
// (see mouse.domain).
// Source: Space Station 14 (MIT), `DragonCarpCompound` / `KillerTomatoCompound` (melee > follow > idle) in
// Resources/Prototypes/NPCs/mob.yml at commit 614f030530578e248a2393dd71ee9813d68d800d:
// https://github.com/space-wizards/space-station-14/blob/614f030530578e248a2393dd71ee9813d68d800d/Resources/Prototypes/NPCs/mob.yml
// Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2017-2026 Space Wizards Federation; see src/examples/canon/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
// Adapted (YAML prototypes re-written in our domain language).
// Emulations: SS14 keeps the leader in the blackboard key `FollowTarget`; here the host writes `(leader ?entity)`.
// Deviations: guards on the root branches.
// Not ported: `RatServantTargetAttackCompound` (a servant that attacks what its leader orders: `regalrat.yml`'s
// order dispatch belongs to a `minion_orders` example).
//
// Facts:      (leader ?entity); see the tiers for the rest. Primitives: see the tiers.

(:domain PetFollower top_level_domain

    (:method (behave) top_level_method

        (fight
            (and
                (#melee_target ?target)
            )
            (
                (melee ?target)
            )
        )

        (follow
            (and
                (leader ?leader)
            )
            (
                (follow ?leader)
            )
        )

        (idle
            ()
            (
                (idle)
            )
        )
    )
)
